    p("70:30","spousal-relation",[("eşleri",3),("yle",2)],"Ala azwajihim in the guarding exception is expressed by Turkish eşleriyle, as in reviewed 23:6. This is contextual relation/valency, not a universal instrumental equivalent of ala.")
    d("70:30:2","Restore the spousal relation within its stated exception scope.")
    p("71:26","disbeliever-class",[("kafirler",9),("den",8)],"Min al-kafirina identifies the class in the no-inhabitant request. Expose the existing source/class ending rather than leave it parenthesized at both views.")
    d("71:26:8","Restore the class relation without changing the scope or speaker of the quoted prayer.")
    p("72:5","never-saying-content",[("asla ",4),("söyle",5),("me",4),("yecek",3),("lerini",5)],"An lan taqula nominalizes the thought that humans/jinn would never speak a lie against God. Expose negation and complement nominalization, retaining the plural reported subjects and future scope from the whole lan clause.")
    d("72:5:3","Restore the thought-content nominal, not another copy of the emphatic never adverb.")
    p("72:7","never-raising-content",[("asla ",6),("dirilt",7),("me",6),("yeceğ",5),("ini",7)],"An lan yabatha is the reported never-raising content. Preserve the inherited resurrection reading of bath, exposing nominalization and negation; this does not uniquely exclude the other traditional mission/sending analysis of the verb here.")
    d("72:7:5","Restore the thought-content nominal under the explicitly recorded inherited raising interpretation.")
    p("72:12","cannot-thwart-content",[("asla ",4),("aciz bırak",5),("ama",4),("yacağ",3),("ımızı",5)],"An lan nujiza supplies the recognized inability to thwart God. Preserve the inherited Turkish ability-negative -ama as the contextual force of the whole no-thwarting-on-earth/no-escape clause, not an overt Arabic can morpheme; expose an's nominalization separately.")
    d("72:12:3","Restore content/negation separation while recording the contextual nature of the Turkish inability reading.")
    p("72:28","conveyed-content",[("duyur",4),("duk",2),("larını",4)],"An qad ablaghu gives the known content of completed conveying. Expose nominal-relative -duk at an; certainty remains at qad rather than being copied into an.")
    d("72:28:2","Restore the content nominal without treating an itself as elbette.")
    p("73:20","counting-content",[("asla ",22),("sizin onu say",23),("ama",22),("yacağ",21),("ınızı",23)],"An lan tuhsuhu nominalizes the known inability to keep the night measure precisely. Preserve the inherited contextual ability-negative, distinguishing it from a literal overt Arabic can morpheme and keeping nominalization at an.")
    d("73:20:21","Restore the content nominal and negative scope while leaving the intended night-measure referent in context, not replacing it with a new astronomical claim.")
    p("74:15","increase-complement",[("daha da artır",4),("ma",3),("mı",4)],"An azida is the desired content of My increasing more. Expose the nominalizer and preserve the first-person subject/object inflection of artırmamı.")
    d("74:15:3","Restore the desired-increase complement rather than duplicate the entire nominal at an.")
    p("74:41","criminal-topic",[("suçlular",2),(" hakkında",1)],"An al-mujrimin is the topic about criminals in the preceding mutual questioning. Restore the topic relation and unpossessed noun rather than an unexplained suçluların genitive.")
    d("74:41:1","Restore the about relation across the verse boundary without inventing a new question object.")
    b.extra_ayahs += ["74:40"]
    d("75:12:1 75:12:2 75:12:3","Retain the explicitly inspected Rabbine o gün complementary views: ila supplies the destination case, rabbika the addressed Lord and yawmaidh the day. All views share the same expression and keep their own foreground.",True)
    p("76:1","rhetorical-period-question",[("geç",2),("me",1),("di",2),(" mi?",1)],"Hal ata is the rhetorical question about a preceding period. Preserve the idiomatic Turkish negative question geçmedi mi, which expects affirmation, exposing its interrogative-negation at hal. This does not teach that Arabic hal lexically means not.")
    d("76:1:1","Restore the question contribution and document the Turkish rhetorical polarity choice.")
    p("76:8","despite-love",[("sevme",4),("lerine rağmen",3)],"Ala hubbihi under the feeding clause is read with the supplied English as despite loving the food. Restore the concession omitted by the bare relative sevdikleri. The beloved-food pronoun interpretation is selected, not claimed to exhaust the attested love-of-God reading.")
    d("76:8:3","Restore the concessive relation under the explicitly recorded inherited beloved-food reading.")
    for ay in ["79:15","85:17","88:1"]:
        p(ay,"reached-question",[("sana geldi",2),(" mi?",1)],"Hal asks whether the account reached the addressee. Expose the question particle separately from the coming predicate.")
        d(f"{ay}:1","Restore the interrogative contribution without duplicating the whole question.")
    d("80:18:2","Retain the inspected hangi şeyden phrase: ayyi supplies hangi, shay thing and min its source case. Their current complementary views already expose those functions.",True)
    p("84:4","contents-relative",[("içinde",3),("kileri",2)],"Ma fiha identifies what the earth contains and casts out. Expose the relative/object ending rather than copy the complete içindekileri at ma.")
    d("84:4:2","Restore the relative contents without changing the earth's casting-out action.")
    p("84:14","never-return-content",[("hiç ",4),("dön",5),("me",4),("yeceğ",3),("ini",5)],"An lan yahura is the imagined never-returning content. Expose nominalization and negation, preserving the reported singular subject and the eschatological return context.")
    d("84:14:3","Restore the thought-content nominal rather than copy the never adverb.")
    p("84:22","relative-disbelievers",[("inkar ed",3),("enler",2)],"Alladhina kafaru identifies those who disbelieve. Expose the plural relative ending rather than duplicate the lexical noun inkarcılar.")
    d("84:22:2","Restore source-relative contribution without changing the following denial predicate.")
    d("85:7:2","Under the inherited Turkish seyretmek paraphrase of shuhud, what they do is a direct object. Ala's witness/topic relation is absorbed by that valency; retain the contextual view rather than impose a literal physical-over phrase. The alternative witness rendering is not denied.",True)
    p("86:11","possessing-return",[("dönüş",3),("lü",2)],"Dhat al-raj describes the sky as possessing return. Turkish dönüşlü exposes the possession adjective suffix at dhat; this local rendering does not specify a scientific atmospheric mechanism or uniquely settle the rain interpretation of raj.")
    d("86:11:2","Restore the possessor-adjective relation without adding a new physical-science claim.")
    p("90:14","famine-day",[("kıtlığ",6),("ın hüküm sürdüğü",5)],"Dhi masghabatin characterizes a day of severe hunger. Turkish kıtlığın hüküm sürdüğü expresses the possessed temporal condition, with normal k-to-ğ stem alternation; the verbal phrase is contextual Turkish realization of the noun relation, not an extra Arabic event verb.")
    d("90:14:5","Restore the severe-hunger day relation rather than leave dhi as a copy of açlık.")
